{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>If you do not heed Me.</b> He suspended the matter upon hearing, which is Torah, for one is prevented from returning in repentance except by means of Torah." "<b>Seven for your sins.</b> Meaning, corresponding to the measure of their sins, which are seven, measure for measure, and these are the seven transgressions: 1 — they did not heed; 2 — they did not do; 3 — they despised My statutes; 4 — they abhorred the judgments of HaShem; 5 — they prevent others from doing; 6 — they violated the covenant; and after HaShem disciplined them and they did not heed Him and they locked the gates of repentance — behold, this is 7. And for this reason we settle the statement of our Sages of blessed memory who said (Rosh HaShanah 16b): three books are opened on Rosh HaShanah, etc.; the intermediate ones hang in the balance, etc. until Yom HaKippurim, etc. — end quote. Meaning, because HaShem suspended them to do repentance and they did not do it, their weight was tipped to the side of the wicked."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:09.061970465Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}